    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for suseconnect-ng",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for suseconnect-ng fixes the following issue:\n\n- Build against outdated `go1.24-openssl` (bsc#1268900).\n\nChanges for suseconnect-ng:\n\n- Update version to 1.23.0:\n  - Use product identifier for product migrations (bsc#1268596).\n  - Switch to using `go1.26-openssl` as the default Go version to install to support building the package\n    (bsc#1268900).\n  - Fix flag parsing so that unknown flags or options are flagged as an error and the usage message is displayed\n    (bsc#1159776).\n  - `InstallReleasePackage` interactive/noninteractive handling should be consistent with `DistUpgrade` (bsc#1267478).\n  - Add new optional `rpm_packages collector`, disabled by default, to collect list of installed SUSE vendored RPM\n    packages.\n  - Allow deregsiter when subscribed `regcode` has expired (bsc#1270392).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SLE-Micro-6.1-671",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
